<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Java on Ruoke Zhang</title><link>https://ruokezhang.github.io/en/tags/java/</link><description>Recent content in Java on Ruoke Zhang</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 18 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://ruokezhang.github.io/en/tags/java/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Java Reflection &amp; Dynamic Proxy</title><link>https://ruokezhang.github.io/en/post/java-reflection-dynamic-proxy/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ruokezhang.github.io/en/post/java-reflection-dynamic-proxy/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="reflection">Reflection
&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#reflection">&lt;/a>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Reflection is Java&amp;rsquo;s ability to dynamically &lt;strong>obtain class information&lt;/strong> (such as class names, methods, properties, constructors, etc.) and &lt;strong>manipulate classes&lt;/strong> at &lt;strong>runtime&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="api">API
&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#api">&lt;/a>
&lt;/h3>&lt;h4 id="getting-class-objects">Getting Class Objects
&lt;a class="header-anchor" href="#getting-class-objects">&lt;/a>
&lt;/h4>&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div style="color:#4c4f69;background-color:#eff1f5;-moz-tab-size:2;-o-tab-size:2;tab-size:2;">
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">&lt;tr>&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">
